# Anything that a Linux box executes or parses must keep LF endings. Checked
# out on Windows these would otherwise become CRLF, and a stray \r turns a
# shell script into "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" and a systemd unit into a
# service that will not start — both with errors that name the wrong cause.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
